Charles Gibson)  The search by Congress for a plan to rescue the economy introduced.  \n\n(Capitol Hill: Jake Tapper)  The growing opposition to the bailout legislation examined; details given about the issue of executive compensation.  [Senators Jim DeMINT, Sherrod BROWN&#134;, Representative Deborah PRYCE&#134;, Senator Charles SCHUMER&#134;, Representative Steven LaTOURETTE&#134;- question the bailout plan proposals.]  [Federal Reserve Board chairman Ben BERNANKE&nbsp- outlines the likely outcome in the economy.]  [Treasury Secretary Henry PAULSON&nbsp- says Americans are angry about executive compensation.]  Earlier bailout requests from President Bush's administration reviewed.  [DeMINT&nbsp- says Paulson has lost credibility.]  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Bush's address tonight to make the case for rescuing the economy announced.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson; Washington: George Stephanopoulos)  The negative reaction to the rescue plan, the need to build on the deal between the administration and Congress, what the president will likely say tonight in his address about the nation's economic security discussed.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  ABC News coverage of the speech noted.  Stock Market Report.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson, Betsy Stark)  The reaction of the stock market after billionaire Warren Buffett announced he was buying 5 billion in stock in Goldman Sachs and the Wall Street support for the Paulson plan discussed.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  The large lead for Senator Barack Obama over Senator John McCain in the latest ABC News/\"Washington Post\" poll to the economy issue cited. ", "segment_duration": 610, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905560, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "1t5H6fef5K", "broadc